{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "def is_woodall(n):\n    \"\"\"Check if n is a Woodall number (n * 2^n - 1 for some positive integer n).\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return False\n    \n    # Try different values of k to see if n = k * 2^k - 1\n    k = 1\n    while k * (2 ** k) - 1 <= n:\n        if k * (2 ** k) - 1 == n:\n            return True\n        k += 1\n        if k > 64:  # Reasonable upper bound to avoid infinite loop\n            break\n    \n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "def find_Max_Num(digits):\n    # Convert digits to strings and sort in descending order based on custom comparison\n    str_digits = [str(d) for d in digits]\n    \n    # Custom sort: compare a+b vs b+a to determine which should come first\n    from functools import cmp_to_key\n    \n    def compare(x, y):\n        if x + y > y + x:\n            return -1\n        elif x + y < y + x:\n            return 1\n        else:\n            return 0\n    \n    str_digits.sort(key=cmp_to_key(compare))\n    return int(''.join(str_digits))"}
