{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    \"\"\"Find the largest sum of contiguous subarray in array repeated k times.\"\"\"\n    if k == 1:\n        max_ending_here = max_so_far = arr[0]\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            max_ending_here = max(arr[i], max_ending_here + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n        return max_so_far\n    \n    # Calculate max subarray sum for single array\n    max_kadane = float('-inf')\n    curr_max = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        curr_max = max(arr[i], curr_max + arr[i])\n        max_kadane = max(max_kadane, curr_max)\n    \n    # Calculate prefix and suffix sums\n    prefix_sum = float('-inf')\n    curr_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        curr_sum += arr[i]\n        prefix_sum = max(prefix_sum, curr_sum)\n    \n    suffix_sum = float('-inf')\n    curr_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n        curr_sum += arr[i]\n        suffix_sum = max(suffix_sum, curr_sum)\n    \n    # Total sum of array\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n    \n    # If total sum is positive, we can benefit from middle repetitions\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        return max(max_kadane, prefix_sum + suffix_sum + (k-2) * total_sum)\n    else:\n        return max(max_kadane, prefix_sum + suffix_sum)"}
