{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find maximum sum of increasing subsequence ending at index i, then including element at index k\n    dp_prefix = [0] * n\n    dp_prefix[0] = arr[0]\n    \n    # Calculate maximum increasing subsequence sum up to each position\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        dp_prefix[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[j]:\n                dp_prefix[j] = max(dp_prefix[j], dp_prefix[prev] + arr[j])\n    \n    # Find maximum sum ending at or before index i, then add element at index k if valid\n    max_sum_at_i = max(dp_prefix[:i+1])\n    \n    # Check if we can extend with element at index k\n    result = max_sum_at_i\n    for j in range(i+1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            result = max(result, dp_prefix[j] + arr[k])\n    \n    return result"}
