{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    \"\"\"Set the leftmost unset bit in the binary representation of n.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Find the position of the leftmost unset bit\n    temp = n\n    bit_position = 0\n    \n    # Find the highest set bit position\n    while temp:\n        temp >>= 1\n        bit_position += 1\n    \n    # Check each bit from left to right to find first unset bit\n    for i in range(bit_position, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n    \n    # If all bits are set, set the next higher bit\n    return n | (1 << bit_position)"}
